.TH "OES_ELEMENT_INDEX_UINT" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
OES_element_index_uint \- OES_element_index_uint extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]OES_element_index_uint\f[B]\f[R] extension is part of the
WebGL API and adds support for \f[CR]gl.UNSIGNED_INT\f[R] types to
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.drawElements()\f[R].
.PP
WebGL extensions are available using the
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getExtension()\f[R] method.
For more information, see Using WebGL extensions.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This extension is only available to WebGL1 contexts.
In WebGL2, the functionality of this extension is available on the
WebGL2 context by default.
.RE
.SH EXTENDED METHODS
This extension extends \f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.drawElements()\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]type\f[R] parameter now accepts \f[CR]gl.UNSIGNED_INT\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] ext = gl.getExtension(\(dqOES_element_index_uint\(dq);

gl.drawElements(gl.POINTS, 8, gl.UNSIGNED_INT, 0);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getExtension()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.drawElements()\f[R]
